<title>NORWAY: TABLE - Christiania Bank H1 profits rise.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Christiania Bank H1 profits rise.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30.</p>
<p>				(millions of crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Net interest income	1,737     vs    1,704</p>
<p>Operating profit before</p>
<p>loan losses and profit</p>
<p> on long-term securities  1,050     vs	978</p>
<p> Operating profit	   1,233     vs    1,111</p>
<p> Net profit		   1,210     vs    1,099</p>
<p> EPS (crowns)		  2.20     vs     2.00</p>
<p>NOTE -- Full name of Norway's second biggest bank is Christiania Bank og Kreditkasse ASA. It was expected to post a first-half 1997 pre-tax operating profit of about 1.25 billion crowns, according to six analysts polled by Reuters.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
